  "final_message": "Declined payments are now retried. The cause was in `due_for_retry` in `billing/dunning.py`.\n\nThat function looked for invoices with status `\"opened\"`, but the real status value is `\"open\"`. No invoice ever matched, so nothing was retried. `next_attempt_at` stayed in the past and the subscription stayed `past_due`, never recovering or becoming `unpaid`. I changed the comparison to `\"open\"`.\n\nThe 24 tests pass and mypy reports no issues. I didn't add a test that covers this bug, so the existing tests don't exercise the fix.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repo root:\n```json\n{\"file\": \"dunning.py\", \"function\": \"due_for_retry\"}\n```",
